{#
    The main menu, one entry per entity of the schema.

    IT IS INCLUDED FROM THE LAYOUT'S `nav` BLOCK, not from a single page, so every view of
    epic 002 gets the navigation without bringing it along. A page that must not show it — the
    sign-in mask — simply leaves that block unfilled.

    THE ITEMS COME READY-MADE from `View\MenuBuilder::build()`: label, entity name and URL are
    decided there, because the mapping from an entity name to a URL segment has an inverse that
    story 002-003 needs (ADR 0011), and a rule split between a template and a class is a rule
    that drifts.

    THE LINKS LEAD NOWHERE UNTIL STORY 002-003 mounts the list route — that is known and
    accepted, so that 002-003 only adds the route instead of touching the menu a second time.
#}
<nav class="admin-nav" aria-label="Hauptmenü">
    <ul class="admin-nav__list">
{% for item in menu %}
        <li class="admin-nav__item"><a class="admin-nav__link" href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.label }}</a></li>
{% endfor %}
    </ul>

    <a class="admin-nav__logout" href="{{ logoutUrl }}">Abmelden</a>
</nav>
